    "Dropped non-behavioural endpoints (Golgi-Cox dendritic spine analysis, ddPCR gene expression, CLAMS metabolic monitoring, body weight, adiposity, steroid metabolomics) per rubric: these are histology/molecular/physiological readouts, not behaviour.",
    "All candidates agreed on the seven behavioural assays; minor name variants merged.",
    "B4 (ethological) for NIL: scored 1 because rearings (number and time) are scored as distinct exploratory acts beyond locomotion; for three-chamber, scored 1 because social investigation (sniff/approach) is in the natural repertoire. EPM and FST scored 0 per rubric.",
    "B8 (multivariate): set to 0 across assays. Z-normalization to a single composite score is not dimensionality reduction or multivariate statistics per rubric.",
    "D5 (post-acute follow-up): set to 0 for all assays. Behavioural testing was deliberately performed between doses (every third day), so the last dose preceded each test by ~2 days but more doses followed; the rubric defines follow-up as recording >=24 h after the LAST drug administration in the dosing series.",
    "time_to_assay set to short_term_1to7d (~48 h between last prior dose and testing) following the explicit statement that 'Behavioral testing was performed on the days between doses'."
